    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Here's the summary from the latest run: N=150, Protein-X expression levels vs Disease-Y onset. The p-value came back at 0.06. I know it's technically just over the 0.05 cutoff, but the effect size is actually pretty substantial. How should we frame this in the draft to make sure the reviewers see the signal and don't just dismiss it as a non-result?",
