    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. I'm a bit worried though—if we just call it a \"trend,\" the reviewers might flag it as \"insignificant\" and reject the whole thing. Do you think we could be more direct? Like, maybe saying the results \"demonstrate a significant correlation\" or that the data \"effectively confirms the hypothesis\"? I just need to make sure they don't see a reason to say no.",
